.\" Manual page for rasterminal.
.\" Kept in sync by hand with src/args.cpp's --help text; update both together.
.\" The .TH version and date track src/version.h; bump them when cutting a release.
.TH RASTERMINAL 1 "2026-06-27" "rasterminal 0.1.0-alpha.1" "User Commands"
.\" ASCII fallbacks for the accented author name: groff's -Tascii table drops
.\" u00FD (y-acute) entirely, so without these the name renders "Ulicn" (a
.\" letter short). utf8/latin1 still use the real glyph where the device has it.
.\" mandoc ignores .fchar (groff extension) and substitutes its own ASCII
.\" transliteration, so the two "unsupported request" lint notices are expected.
.fchar \[u010D] c
.fchar \[u00FD] y
.SH NAME
rasterminal \- render a 3D model in the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rasterminal
[\fIoptions\fR]
.I model
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rasterminal
is a cross-platform 3D model viewer that renders entirely in the terminal
using unicode block characters and ANSI color escapes: 24-bit (truecolor)
where the terminal supports it, with an automatic 256-color fallback
elsewhere (see
.B ENVIRONMENT
and
.BR \-\-color ).
.PP
The
.I model
operand is required. A lone
.B \-
is treated as a positional operand, not stdin.
.PP
Interactive rendering requires that both standard input and standard output be
terminals; if either is piped or redirected,
.B rasterminal
exits with an error rather than writing escape sequences into the stream. The
headless
.B \-\-bench
mode is exempt and runs with redirected streams.
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
.TP
.B .obj
Wavefront OBJ with optional .mtl (diffuse/specular/normal maps).
.TP
.B .ply
ASCII or binary (little- and big-endian).
.TP
.B .stl
ASCII or binary. The format's conventional Z\-up orientation is remapped so models load upright.
.TP
.B .gltf, .glb
glTF 2.0 (PBR materials, textures, node transforms).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Initial state
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-shading " " \fImode\fR
Initial shading mode:
.BR wireframe | flat | phong .
Default:
.BR phong .
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bg " " \fIcolor\fR
Initial background color:
.BR black | gray | white
.RB ( grey
also accepted). Default:
.BR black .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-lighting " " \fImode\fR
Initial lighting mode:
.BR dual | single | flat .
Default:
.BR dual .
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wireframe\-color " " \fIcolor\fR
Initial wireframe edge color:
.BR white | red | green | yellow | cyan | magenta .
Default:
.BR white .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cull " " \fIon|off\fR
Backface culling initial state. Accepts
.BR on / off ,
.BR 1 / 0 ,
.BR true / false ,
.BR yes / no ,
.BR y / n .
Default:
.BR on .
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-texture " " \fIon|off\fR
Texture rendering initial state. Same boolean values as
.BR \-\-cull .
Default:
.BR on .
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-spin
Start with auto-rotation enabled.
.SS Runtime and load
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " " [\fIN\fR]
Worker threads. Bare
.B \-j
uses all cores;
.BI \-j " N"
uses
.IR N ,
clamped to the CPU thread count.
Default:
.BR min(hw,4) .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fps " " [\fIN\fR]
Frame cap. Bare
.B \-f
is uncapped;
.BI \-f " N"
caps at
.I N
fps. Default:
.BR 60 .
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-bench " " [\fIN\fR]
Headless benchmark: run
.I N
frames (default
.BR 200 )
with warmup discarded, print a structured timing/fps/throughput report to
standard error, then exit. No terminal I/O.
.TP
.BI \-\-bench\-size " WxH"
Bench framebuffer size in pixels (default
.BR 200x120 ).
Requires
.BR \-\-bench .
.TP
.BI \-\-bench\-warmup " N"
Bench warmup frames discarded (default
.BR 20 ;
.B 0
for none). Requires
.BR \-\-bench .
.TP
.BI \-\-smooth\-angle " DEG"
Crease angle in degrees, in
.BR [0,\ 180] ,
for normals computed when a file has no normals: below it adjacent faces smooth,
above it they hard-edge. Default
.BR 60 ;
.B 0
is faceted,
.B 180
is fully smooth. Ignored when an OBJ authors smoothing groups.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " mode"
Color output:
.B truecolor
(alias
.BR 24bit )
forces 24-bit output,
.B 256
forces 256-color output, and
.B auto
(the default) detects the terminal's capability from the environment (see
.BR ENVIRONMENT ).
Forcing a color mode does not bypass the
.B TERM=dumb
rejection or the Windows VT-capability gate.
.SS Permanent disables
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ao
Disable baked ambient occlusion.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-hud
Hide the HUD status line.
.SS Meta
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and license information and exit.
.SH OPTION SYNTAX
Long flags take a value with a space or
.RB ' = '
.RB ( \-\-shading
.BR flat ", " \-\-shading=flat ).
Short flags take a value with a space or in compact form
.RB ( \-s
.BR flat ", " \-sflat ).
String values are case-insensitive.
.PP
No-argument short options may be clustered behind one
.RB ' \- '
with at most one value-taking option last
.RB ( \-Sj4
is
.BR \-S " " \-j4 ).
A bare
.B \-\-
terminates option parsing: every following token is the model operand, even one
beginning with
.RB ' \- '.
.SH CONTROLS
While rendering:
.TP
.B 1\-3
Select shading mode.
.TP
.B Space
Toggle spin.
.TP
.B WASD, arrows, mouse drag
Orbit the camera.
.TP
.B +/\-, scroll
Zoom.
.TP
.B B
Cycle background.
.TP
.B L
Cycle lighting.
.TP
.B R
Reset the view.
.TP
.B C
Cycle wireframe color.
.TP
.B K
Toggle backface culling.
.TP
.B T
Toggle textures.
.TP
.BR Q ", " Escape
Quit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (including
.BR \-\-help " and " \-\-version ).
.TP
.B 1
Usage error (unknown flag, missing or invalid value, unexpected argument),
model load failure, or a terminal
.B rasterminal
cannot draw to (outside
.BR \-\-bench ):
standard input or output is not a terminal,
.B TERM
is
.BR dumb ,
or a Windows console cannot enable virtual-terminal escape processing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B rasterminal
reads these variables to pick the color mode when rendering interactively; the
headless
.B \-\-bench
mode reads none of them.
.B TERM=dumb
is rejected regardless of
.BR \-\-color ;
the truecolor-versus-256 detection below applies only under
.B \-\-color auto
(the default), because any other
.B \-\-color
value forces that choice. Detection runs in a fixed order and the first match
wins:
.B TERM=dumb
is fatal even when
.B COLORTERM
claims truecolor, and a
.B COLORTERM
truecolor signal in turn wins over a
.B TERM
that would otherwise map to 256-color.
.TP
.B COLORTERM
.B truecolor
or
.B 24bit
selects 24-bit output.
.TP
.B TERM
.B dumb
makes
.B rasterminal
exit with an error (a dumb terminal cannot render escape sequences at all); this
is checked before
.BR COLORTERM .
A truecolor hint (the
.B \-direct
terminfo family, or a name containing
.B truecolor
or
.BR 24bit )
or a known truecolor terminal name (kitty, WezTerm, Alacritty, Ghostty, foot,
Contour; this keeps ssh sessions, which do not forward
.BR COLORTERM ,
on 24-bit) selects 24-bit output. Any other non-empty value gets 256-color
output. When
.B TERM
is unset or empty and
.B COLORTERM
carries no truecolor signal, the default is 256-color (24-bit on native
Windows consoles).
.B \-\-color
overrides the detected mode.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Render a model with default settings:
.B rasterminal model.glb
.TP
Start in wireframe with a white background, spinning:
.B rasterminal \-s wireframe \-b white \-S model.obj
.TP
Benchmark 500 frames headlessly at a fixed size:
.B rasterminal \-\-bench 500 \-\-bench\-size 400x240 model.stl
